[00:00.78]Lesson 4 | 第4课
[00:02.44]The double life of Alfred Bloggs | 阿尔弗雷德·布洛格斯的双重生活
[00:11.34]Why did Alf want a white-collar job? | 阿尔夫为什么想要一份白领工作？
[00:16.83]These days, people who do manual work often receive far more money than people who work in offices. | 如今，从事体力劳动的人的收入往往远远高于坐办公室的人。
[00:24.76]People who work in offices are frequently referred to as 'white-collar workers' for the simple reason that they usually wear a collar and tie to go to work. | 坐办公室的人之所以常常被称作“白领工人”，原因很简单：他们上班时通常穿硬领、系领带。
[00:36.74]Such is human nature, that a great many people are often willing to sacrifice higher pay for the privilege of becoming white-collar workers. | 许多人常常宁愿放弃较高的薪水以换取做白领工人的殊荣，人性就是如此。
[00:48.19]This can give rise to curious situations, as it did in the case of Alfred Bloggs who worked as a dustman for the Ellesmere Corporation. | 这可能会引起种种奇怪的情形，在埃尔兹米尔公司当清洁工的阿尔弗雷德·布洛格斯便是其中一例。
[01:00.78]When he got married, Alf was too embarrassed to say anything to his wife about his job. | 阿尔夫结婚时，因为难为情，甚至没有对自己的妻子讲过自己的职业。
[01:07.63]He simply told her that he worked for the Corporation. | 他只说自己供职于公司。
[01:11.57]Every morning, he left home dressed in a smart black suit. | 每天早晨，他穿一身漂亮的黑西装离家。
[01:16.45]He then changed into overalls and spent the next eight hours as a dustman. | 然后换上工装裤，当8个小时的清洁工。
[01:22.90]Before returning home at night, he took a shower and changed back into his suit. | 晚上回家前，他洗个淋浴，重新换上西装。
[01:29.02]Alf did this for over two years and his fellow dustmen kept his secret. | 阿尔夫这样干了两年多，清洁工的同事们为他保密。
[01:35.66]Alf's wife has never discovered that she married a dustman and she never will, for Alf has just found another job. | 阿尔夫的妻子从未发现自己嫁了个清洁工，而且永远也不会发现了，因为阿尔夫刚找了份新工作。
[01:44.47]He will soon be working in an office. | 他不久就要坐在办公室里工作了。
[01:47.61]He will be earning only half as much as he used to, but he feels that his rise in status is well worth the loss of money. | 他挣的钱将只有过去的一半，但他觉得地位升高了，损失点钱也完全值得。
[01:57.05]From now on, he will wear a suit all day and others will call him 'Mr.Bloggs', not 'Alf'. | 从今以后，他将整天穿西装，别人会叫他“布洛格斯先生”，而不是“阿尔夫”了。
